WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:02.735
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Cecily Strong.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.138
So, this is a memoir
that you wrote this year

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.174
about sort of the anxiety
and how difficult it was

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:11.011
to get through the pandemic
and also a very difficult

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.446
personal thing,
and my condolences,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.782
your cousin, Owen, passed away.
-Yes.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.082
-Very young and very tragically.

00:00:17.082 --> 00:00:21.254
-Yeah, he was 30,
and we lost him in January 2020

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:25.625
to glioblastoma, and I didn't
really start grieving it

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.826
and was back at work

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.995
and didn't know how to
talk about it really.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:33.733
And then the world shut down,
and I had all this time

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:38.204
to sort of -- but wound up
being a gift sort of --

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.206
it was like I was trying to
find out

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:44.143
how Owen lived so well
with glioblastoma.

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:48.247
Like, my favorite of his quotes
is he told his dad, "You know,

00:00:48.247 --> 00:00:51.150
Minus the brain cancer, this has
been the best year of my life."

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.551
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:55.021
And he was, you know, just
a very positive person.

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:59.859
And so I have -- in trying to
figure that out,

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.461
how he lived so well,
was sort of --

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:06.199
I had the best navigator through
COVID about just sort of

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.935
having positivity or optimism

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.070
and hope kind of
as an active choice.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.139
-I think it's a real gift
to readers right now,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.974
who I think a lot of people,
obviously,

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.975
have had to deal with loss
over the past year,

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:20.479
and this is dealt with in
such a sincere but funny way.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:22.581
Was it also cathartic
to write it?

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:24.417
-I mean, so much so.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.554
It was -- I was looking back
to see pictures on my phone

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:31.157
actually from March to August
or something.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:36.262
And I was so shocked at how
many, like, pictures and videos

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:38.030
of us dancing or having fun.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.300
I was like, "Oh, I had fun too,
I guess."

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.002
And I think because I would
write during the day

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.471
and sort of go through that

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.306
and then we'd have
our little family dinner,

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:50.209
and Kevin would read --
not the woodchuck Kevin,

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:54.480
Kevin my human dear friend,
would read at the table.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.949
And we'd, like, cry and sort of
talk about it

00:01:56.949 --> 00:02:00.186
and then have a dance party.
-Very nice.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.255
-Yeah, it was really great.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:06.025
-I want to also commend you
on another fantastic year.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:09.162
An Emmy nominated for you year,
well-deserved.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:12.465
-I think I was so proud of
that whole show.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.066
-It was amazing
what you guys pulled off.

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.836
-Everybody being there
and doing what we did has, like,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.472
kept us all standing
and kept us going.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.840
-It was so massively different
than anything experienced.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.309
I would just roll down --
every now and then

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.110
I walked down the hall, I mean,
the fact you guys were doing

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:27.547
a table read in the studio, and
just everybody is spread out.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.949
It's usually, like, this really
intensely close experience,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.817
and yet, it still felt
incredibly intimate

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:33.285
when you watch the show.

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:35.254
This, hard to pull off
in a non-pandemic.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:39.092
You did Jeanine Pirro,
and she sang from a box of wine.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.026
-Yeah.
-How did this idea come about?

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:42.728
-Well, Tucker texted me --

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.398
Brian Tucker is a writer,
and he texted me that week like,

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:48.834
"Do you want to do a
Jeanine Pirro singing 'My Way,'"

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.869
but he wrote it "moy wa."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.869 --> 00:02:54.207
And I was like, "Sure,
but we have to --"

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.175
You know, I always want to
up the ante.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:59.312
It's become
a very fun, physical thing,

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:03.115
and last time,
I threw up red wine on Colin.

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.551
So I was like,
"Well, then I have to be

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.653
in a box of wine or something."

00:03:07.653 --> 00:03:10.423
And then what's fun about "SNL"
is you tell them this,

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.992
and then they make it happen,
but yeah, so then I looked up --

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.059
-You sent this to them?

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:15.128
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.863
When they say,
"How do you do that?"

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.932
I was like, "Well, like this."

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:22.634
So, this man is bleeding
and in chains.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:25.171
So I said, "Just without
the blood and the chains."

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.606
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.808
-And it worked out.
-It worked out.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:34.480
-I texted Colin because you
and Colin wrote "The girl

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.182
you wish you weren't having
a conversation with at a party."

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:37.817
And that was the first time
you were on "Update,"

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:42.121
and I remember being in awe of
you at that moment.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.692
And I was watching, like --
Colin was, like, so --

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.093
At one point he was just shaking
his head like,

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:51.464
"I cannot believe
how out of sight this is."

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:54.066
-It's also I've never --
I feel, like, that's, like,

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:55.902
a hidden side of Colin
that people don't know,

00:03:55.902 --> 00:04:00.006
is that he loves to be,
like, beaten up or something.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:03.075
Like, he loves having things
thrown on him.

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:05.311
At one point I was like --
-He ended up with Black Widow.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.812
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:11.284
She hits him every day.
It's okay. It's consensual.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.519
-But it was such a delight.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:16.989
And congratulations as well
on "Schmigadoon!"

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.025
We've had a bunch of
your co-stars on the show.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.159
They seem to have had
a great time.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.527
Was it as much fun to make?

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:23.262
-It was so much fun.

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:26.499
But I'm having even more fun
watching the show.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:29.501
I think I watch it entirely --

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:32.905
the entire thing at least twice
a week or something.

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.941
And I got to the point where I'm
like -- it's, like, I'm watching

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:37.777
and saying their lines
along with them,

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.979
especially Kristin, who I feel,
like, has a lot of, like --

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.181
I like to go,
"Okay, I'll do it."

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.116
And, "Oh, yes, you do!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.619
So it's very fun to sing along.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:49.088
-Congratulations on that.
Thanks for being here.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.257
"This Will All Be Over Soon"
is out now.

